/* Versioned SDK effect contracts. The fourth argument is the required effect,
 * not an assertion inferred from a function's spelling. IDs are wire identities:
 * append only, never rename or reuse an existing ID. Only these reviewed runtime operations may
 * execute from a managed task without entering a native callback domain.
 *
 * Signature: return type followed by zero or more parameter types. v = void,
 * p = address-space-zero pointer, i = i32, q = i64 (also 64-bit size_t/ssize_t),
 * f = llam_fd_t (i64 on Windows, i32 elsewhere), h = llam_handle_t (pointer on
 * Windows, i32 elsewhere). No varargs, non-C calling convention, or ABI-changing
 * parameter/return attributes are allowed. Pointer pointees intentionally do
 * not participate in the native ABI; managedTypeIdentity retains every LLVM
 * ABI attribute for contracts outside this scalar SDK table.
 *
 * Lifecycle/loader mutation, manual blocking-domain transitions, debug writes,
 * and narrow integer ABIs remain outside this profile. Name prefixes grant no
 * effect. Public declarations and these ABI shapes are checked by compiler tests.
 */

